          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: A witness observed on July 3, 2010, starting at 11:50 PM, a white glowing point in the sky that intrigued them. No particular noise was heard during the filmed observation. Of low strangeness and average consistency (single witness), this observation case corresponds exactly to the observation of the International Space Station (ISS) for its first part. For the 2nd and 3rd parts reported, it is a probable observation of undetermined satellites. This case is classified A: observation of the International Space Station (ISS).",
